  "Description": {
    "Cost": 2748567,
    "UIName": "Lindworm",
    "Id": "chassisdef_lindworm_LND-C",
    "Name": "Lindworm",
    "Details": "The C configuration of the Lindworm OmniProtoMech carries two AP Gauss Rifles and is one of only two configurations that truly focus on damage output, since the energy and weight requirements of its Electric Discharge ProtoMech Armor make the Lindworm unsuitable for energy weapons. It is very similar to the missile-armed B configuration, but it is focused on attacking enemy infantry formations and has relatively better endurance.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: OmniProtoMech</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 0.986</color></b>",
    "Icon": "Protomech_Basilisk_Quad"
  },
  "VariantName": "LND-C",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "Squad",
      "OmniProtoMech",
      "ProtoMech",
      "ProtoQuad",
      "Trooper",
      "UsesAmmoSameLocationOnly"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Brawler",
  "YangsThoughts": "The Lindworm is the Society's replacement for the Basilisk Quad, which they couldn't get parts for anymore. They built it from scratch around components they make themselves and doubled the weight, but most of that extra weight went into keeping it just as fast and adding armor. It runs Electric Discharge ProtoMech Armor, which is tough, but its weight and energy demands make the Lindworm a poor fit for energy weapons.",
